    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348-a2">

                <pb facs="0461" n="353" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg353"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to the Earl of
                    Aberdeen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-24"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: In accordance with the request
                    contained in Gen. Montgomery Moore’s dispatch, No. 47, of the 25th August last,
                    I transmitted to the United States Secretary of State a copy of the certified
                    report of the privy council of Canada which was therein contained, respecting
                    reciprocal wrecking privileges in the inland waters contiguous to Canada and the
                    United States.</p>
                <p>I have now the honor to inclose copies of a circular<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d348-f1"/> issued by the Treasury Department on the subject, which I
                    have received from Mr. Gresham, for the information of the Canadian
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d348-f1" n="*" xml:id="d348-f1-content">
                <p>For this inclosure see inclosure to note of October 21 from Mr. Gresham, <ref
                        target="#pg351">page 351</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
